    "$biomes_note": "MODIS MCD12Q1 IGBP classes (MEASURED, via GIBS) -> MATERIAL MIXTURES. Fractions come from the IGBP class DEFINITIONS, which are stated as canopy-cover thresholds: forests >60% tree, woody savanna 30-60%, savanna 10-30%, open shrubland 10-60%, barren <10% vegetated. Each is taken at the midpoint of its defined range and the remainder is the ground beneath. So these are read off the classification, not chosen by eye. A class is a MIXTURE because IGBP classes are definitionally mixtures - 'woody savanna' and 'cropland/natural vegetation mosaic' are not one substance, and pretending otherwise is what made the Amazon and Siberia the same colour."
